      "dcterms:title": "Homological Algebra of Knots and BPS States",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Gukov, Sergei",
        "Stoˇsić, Marko"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20181022",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1112.0030",
      "dcterms:abstract": "It is known that knot homologies admit a physical description as spaces of open BPS states. We study operators and algebras acting on these spaces. This leads to a very rich story, which involves wall crossing phenomena, algebras of closed BPS states acting on spaces of open BPS states, and deformations of Landau-Ginzburg models. One important application to knot homologies is the existence of “colored diﬀerentials” that relate homological invariants of knots colored by diﬀerent representations. Based on this structure, we formulate a list of properties of the colored HOMFLY homology that categoriﬁes the colored HOMFLY polynomial. By calculating the colored HOMFLY homology for symmetric and anti-symmetric representations, we ﬁnd a remarkable “mirror symmetry” between these triply-graded theories.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-1112.0030v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-1112.0030v2"
    }
  ]
